\emph{Data and code availability.} The sweep dataset (13{,}200 \amgcl{} and
5{,}400 \hypre{} solves), the feature extractor, the predictor, and all
figure-generation scripts are released at
\url{https://github.com/mirryou-maker/amg-tuning-crosslib}; \texttt{python
reproduce.py} regenerates every figure and headline number from the released
data. The repository also ships the predictor as a ready-to-use tool
(\texttt{python tools/recommend.py your\_matrix.mtx}) that prints a ranked
short-list of \amgcl{} or \hypre{} configurations, with parameter strings that
paste directly into each solver's runtime interface; the top suggestion is a
heuristic (it solves $\sim\!83$--$89\%$ of unseen matrices and captures a
median $\sim\!43$--$49\%$ of the oracle), so the intended use is to try the top
few and keep the fastest.

\emph{Generative AI disclosure.} In accordance with the ACM Policy on
Authorship, the author discloses the use of an AI coding assistant (Claude
Code, Anthropic) in this work: it assisted in implementing the benchmark
harness, the tiered feature extractor, and the gradient-boosted predictor; in
orchestrating the parameter sweeps and the cross-library build on the compute
cluster; and in drafting and revising this manuscript. All experimental design
decisions, numerical results, and scientific claims were checked by the author
against the released code and data. The AI system is not an author and bears no
responsibility for the content; the author takes full responsibility for all
material herein.
